{"id":"vmad.8","n":"vmad","s":"8","src":{"r":{"pkg":"libvma","ver":"9.8.60-1.el9","repo":"AppStream","url":"https://dl.rockylinux.org/vault/rocky/9.6/AppStream/x86_64/os/Packages/l/libvma-9.8.60-1.el9.x86_64.rpm","path":"/usr/share/man/man8/vmad.8.gz","sha256":"b14b7b28a5a7b04f2629334d0080092f4d16fbd79d5da5ae1a91623bd56c4ea5","date":"05 Nov 2024","origin":"libvma"}},"nopt":{"r":4},"desc":"NVIDIA Messaging Accelerator (VMA) daemon.","r":[["NAME","<p>vmad - NVIDIA Messaging Accelerator (VMA) daemon.</p>"],["SYNOPSIS","<p><b>vmad</b> [--console] [--pid,-p <i>num</i>] [--fid,-f <i>num</i>] [--force-rst] [--verbose,-v <i>level</i>]</p>"],["DESCRIPTION","<p>vmad is the daemon program for vma (7).</p> <p>vmad can be configured using command-line options</p> <p>The options are as follows:</p> <p><b>--console</b> Enable foreground mode.</p> <dl><dt data-o=\"\"><b>--pid,-p </b><i>num</i></dt><dd>Set prime number as maximum of processes per node.</dd><dt data-o=\"\"><b>--fid,-f </b><i>num</i></dt><dd>Set prime number as maximum of sockets per process.</dd><dt data-o=\"\"><b>--force-rst</b></dt><dd>Force internal RST.</dd><dt data-o=\"\"><b>--verbose,-v </b><i>level</i></dt><dd>Output verbose level</dd></dl>"],["SEE ALSO","<p><b>vma</b>(7), <b>vma_stats</b>(8)</p>"],["AUTHORS","<dl><dt>Igor Ivanov &lt;igori@mellanox.com&gt;</dt><dd></dd></dl>"]]}